## Known deviation from the current capture.bash (fixed, fixture NOT regenerated)

This fixture was captured **before** a fix to `capture.bash`'s hostgroup
registration. At capture time, hostgroup 1 pointed at `172.26.0.3:3307` —
the dbdeployer GTID *replica*, a separate mysqld from the writer at
`172.26.0.3:3306` — rather than at the same backend as hostgroup 0, which is
what the task brief specifies ("one backend registered in two hostgroups").
`capture.bash` now registers `${BACKEND_IP}:3306` in both hostgroups.

This fixture was kept as-is rather than re-captured: hostgroup 1 carried no
sysbench traffic under either topology (sysbench only ever connects through
hostgroup 0 as `testuser`'s default_hostgroup), so the two topologies
produce the same connpool series *cardinality* — only the `endpoint` label
value on the (idle) hostgroup-1 connpool series differs (`...:3307` here vs.
`...:3306` with the current script). Row shapes, sample interval, and total
series count are unaffected; this fixture remains valid for sizing
purposes. A future re-capture with the fixed script will show
`endpoint=...:3306,hostgroup=1"}` instead of `:3307`.
